[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged as one issue and marked known: the parser reads dates month
first. Reading every report body against its tenant shows three different problems. One fix will
not close all of them, so each now has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{ parser: `${REPO}/1`, hint: `${REPO}/2`, 'one-day move': `${REPO}/3` }}
/>

## parser: day and month swapped

A day-first tenant books 7 April and the invite says 4 July. The shared parser reads every date
month first. It hits every day-first tenant, through the app, by email and through booking-v2 forms.
This is the bug the queued fix is for.

## hint: booking-v3 tells people to type month first

Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour run booking-v3. Its date field shows the hint
`MM/DD/YYYY`, so people type month first, and the form then reads the date day first. The symptom
looks the same as `parser`, but the parser fix does not touch it: the hint and the form disagree.
Intake tagged these by the reporter's browser, so the `hint` tag misses some and catches others
that are not.

## one-day move: the right date, a day early or late

These reports are not swaps. "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Client in
Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." The desk read them as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`) and files them under `parser` by tenant, so they stay counted there too. A
day-month swap cannot move a date by one day, so this is its own bug, most likely in how the
invite's time zone is applied.

<Callout kind="warn">
Why they were merged: <a href="/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject">decision 0001</a> merges on
subject line alone, and all three problems arrive with the same subjects ("Wrong day on the
invite", "Date is wrong"). Subject tells you the symptom. The tenant, its booking form and the body
tell you the cause.
</Callout>

## How the counts are made

Reports are taken once per id (the export repeats 15 of them), grouped with `causeOf` in
`causes.ts` by tenant locale, channel and booking form, as the desk's own view counts them. The
reports listed in `desk-notes.json` as one-day moves stay counted where they are filed and get
their own row. The table is built from the data at render time.

